  "chapter": {
    "number": 126,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(127) A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Except the Lord build the house, they that build labor in vain: except the Lord keep the city, the watchman watches in vain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "It is vain for you to rise early: you⌃ rise up after resting, you⌃ that eat the bread of grief; while he gives sleep to his beloved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, the inheritance of the Lord, children, the reward of the fruit of the womb.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As arrows in the hand of a mighty man; so are the children of those who were outcasts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man who shall satisfy his desire with them: they shall not be ashamed when they shall speak to their enemies in the gates.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
